{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7aAXbKSxQLM2WsvxMn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The network deviates from the protocol in one way.\n\n**Rule C (cord) has an extra margin of about 3 Gy.** The network escalates only when cord_floor exceeds cord_lim by about 3 Gy or more. When cord_floor is above cord_lim by less than that, it sends the request to planning, though the protocol requires escalation.\n- The cut-off sits between a gap of 3.0 and 3.3 Gy in every case tested. At exactly 3.0 Gy, scores were within about ±1 of zero, so those requests fell on either side.\n- This held at cord_lim = 38, 44, 46 and 50, and across several settings of the other inputs, including PTV volumes of 80, 200, 250 and 400 cc.\n- Examples planned instead of escalated: (cord_lim 45, cord_floor 46), (38, 40.5), (50, 52.5) and (44, 47.0) on the most negative baseline.\n\n**Rules A, B and D follow the protocol** everywhere I tested, including within 0.4–0.5 Gy or cc of each threshold. That covered the corners of the input ranges and the most negative baseline score I found.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"deviates\",\n  \"deviations\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Cord goal below the anatomical floor by less than about 3 Gy: the network plans instead of escalating. It applies rule C only when cord_floor exceeds cord_lim by roughly 3 Gy or more, instead of by any amount. If rule A, B or D applies, the request is still escalated correctly.\",\n      \"condition\": \"(cord_floor - cord_lim > 0.3) and (cord_floor - cord_lim < 3.0) and not (cov > cap) and not ((mand_in_ptv - 0.05 * ptv_vol > 0.1) and (cov > mand_lim)) and (missing == 0)\",\n      \"network_decision\": \"plan\",\n      \"protocol_decision\": \"escalate\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3623,"cache_read_input_tokens":11839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3623},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"984cfb9c-31fd-4950-8bb7-976fd4540bd7","uuid":"a38b645b-11ff-40db-811b-49ea2931a8ba","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:18:45.780Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7aAJSvbVFYN4c9cmK1"}
